spills(V) => not tidy(V). @ "If people spill a lot of food on their clothing, then they are not notably tidy."
clumsy_foodie(V) & goes_out_frequently(V) => spills(V). @ "All clumsy foodies who go out frequently to find new food restaurants to try are people who spill a lot of food on their clothing."
cleanly(V) => tidy(V). @ "If people are cleanly, then they are notably tidy."
values_order(V) => cleanly(V). @ "If people value order and spotlessness, then they are cleanly."
family_prioritizes_order(V) => values_order(V). @ "All people whose families prioritize order and spotlessness themselves value order and spotlessness."
not spills(peter) | cleanly(peter). @ "Peter is either a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing and is cleanly, or a person who does not spill a lot of food on his clothing and is not cleanly"
not cleanly(peter) | spills(peter). @ "Peter is either a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing and is cleanly, or a person who does not spill a lot of food on his clothing and is not cleanly"
? tidy(peter).
